ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{5}(R),$ the vector space of all $5\\times 5$ matrices over $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{5}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5}(R))={5}^{2}=25.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-95220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.ty