e-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R),$ the vector space of all $10\\times 2$ matrices over $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R))=10\\cdot 2=20.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "400"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $15?$\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- ${R}_{15}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $15$\n- ${R}^{15}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3\\times 5}(R))=3\\cdot 5=15.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{15}[t])=15+1=16\\ne 15.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{15})=15.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95226" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $3?$\n\n- ${R}^{2}$\n- ${R}_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{2})=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{2}[t])=2+1=3.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $10?$\n\n- ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{5}(R)$, the vector space of all $5\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- ${R}^{10}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(\\text{R}))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5}(R))={5}^{2}=25\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{10})=10.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-106897" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106897" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_c