ty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-106901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $36?$\n\n- ${R}_{6}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $6$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R),$ the vector space of all $12\\times 3$ matrices over $R$\n- ${R}^{36}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{6}[t])=6+1=7\\ne 36.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{12\\times 3}(R))=12\\cdot 3=36.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{36})=36.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\n- ${ℓ}^{1},$ the vector space of infinite real sequences where the sum of the absolute values of the terms are finite\n- ${R}_{3000}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3\\,000$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{50\\times 60}(R),$ the vector space of all $50\\times 60$ matrices over $R$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${ℓ}^{1}$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following subset of ${ℓ}^{1}$ is linearly independent: \n\n$$\n{{e}_{1},\\,{e}_{2},\\,…,{e}_{n}},\\,n\\in N\n$$\n\nwhere, for each $j\\in {1,2,…,n},$\n\n$$\n{e}_{j}=(0,…,0,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{1,}_{{↑}_{{j}^{\\text{th}}\\text{ position}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0,…).\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{x}_{i}{e}_{i}=0\n$$\n\nif and only if ${x}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of ${ℓ}^{1}$ of size $n,$ which imples that  ${ℓ}^{1}$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${R}_{3000}[t]$ and  ${\\text{M}}_{50\\times 60}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{3000}[t])=3\\,000+1=3\\,001,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{50\\times 60}(R))=50\\cdot 60=3\\,000\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-106916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R),$ the vector space of all $250\\times 100$ matrices over $R$\n- $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n- ${R}_{10}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R)$ and ${R}_{10}[t]$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{250\\times 100}(R))=250\\cdot 100=25\\,000\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11,\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/state.json" "file_sha256" "413fcdf6e3e7078d81e39d698dd046ae900e748b0d4d52c23c2b7257bd22941f"} {"question" "q-95251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072692/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4edd8ed1597cb536cb9241b96b7c0a341fd4c9f62309143d81a8332951561b"} {"question" "q-95251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/